.\" darqos
.\" Copyright (C) 2026 David Arnold
.TH DIDLPYGEN 1 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS User's Manual"
.SH NAME
didlpygen \- generate Python message classes from DIDL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B didlpygen
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.I input
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B didlpygen
reads the intermediate representation (IR) written by
.BR didlc (1)
and generates a Python module with classes to hold, encode and decode
the messages it defines.
.PP
The module contains:
.TP
.I enum classes
One
.B enum.IntEnum
class per DIDL enum.
An enum field defaults to its member with value 0, or to its first
member.
.TP
.I struct classes
One class per DIDL struct, holding its fields.
.TP
.I message classes
For a method
.I x
with a response,
.IB x Request
and
.IB x Response\fR;
for a one-way method,
.IR x .
Each has a constructor taking
.B txid
followed by its fields,
.B encode()
returning the message as
.BR bytes ,
with the list of handles to transfer with it,
and
.BI decode( buffer ", " handles )
filling the object from a buffer holding the whole message, and the
handles transferred with it.
A
.B port
field holds a handle, or
.B None
for no port.
.B decode()
raises
.B darq.errors.MessageDecodingError
if the buffer is too short, the method number doesn't match, the
flags are wrong, an opaque value is out of range or not 8-byte
aligned, a port index is past the end of the handles, or an enum
field's value isn't one of its members.
Each request class's
.B RESPONSE
is its response class;
.B None
for a one-way message.
.TP
.I protocol classes
One class per protocol, whose
.B REQUESTS
and
.B RESPONSES
dictionaries map method numbers to message classes.
It holds two nested classes, built on
.BR darq.system ,
each with a method per protocol method, named in snake case
.RB ( GetAttributes
becomes
.BR get_attributes ):
.B Client
takes a service's handle, and its methods take the request's fields,
and return the response;
.B Handler
is the base class for a service's handler, for
.BR darq.serve() ,
and its methods take the request and the client's handle, and return
the response.
.PP
The module contains no boilerplate: the struct and message classes
derive from
.B Record
and
.B Message
in
.BR darq.dipc ,
which also provides
.B decode_method()
and
.B decode_txid()
to read a message header for dispatching.
Struct and message objects compare equal when their fields are equal.
.SS Wire format
Fields are little-endian, at the offsets given in the IR.
The body follows the 8-byte header.
An
.B opaque
field is an 8-byte descriptor: a
.B uint32
offset of its value from the start of the message, then a
.B uint32
length.
The values are appended after the fixed part of the message, in field
order, each starting on an 8-byte boundary and padded with zeros to a
multiple of 8 bytes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output\fR, " \-\-output " output"
Write the module to
.IR output ,
or to standard output if
.I output
is
.BR \- .
By default, it is written next to
.IR input ,
named after the DIDL library with dots replaced by underscores: the
library
.B storage.filesystem
produces
.IR storage_filesystem.py .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the input can't be read, isn't valid IR, has a
format version this
.B didlpygen
doesn't support, or can't
be generated; 2 if the command line is invalid.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are reported on standard error as
.IB file ": error: " message\fR.
Generation fails if a name isn't a valid Python identifier, if two
classes would have the same name, or if a name is one the module
defines itself (such as
.B Message
or
.BR Record ,
which it imports).
Two methods of a protocol may not have the same name in snake case, nor
one the
.B Client
and
.B Handler
base classes use, such as
.B call
or
.BR dispatch .
.SH BUGS
Message class names are not qualified by protocol, so two protocols in
one library can't both have a method with the same name.
.PP
Field values are not range-checked before encoding: an out-of-range
value raises
.BR struct.error .
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
didlc filesystem.didl
didlpygen filesystem.dir
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR didlc (1)
